      textEn: 'I always thought old age would be a writer\u2019s best chance. Whenever I read the late work of Goethe or W. B. Yeats I had the impertinence to identify with it. Now, my memory\u2019s gone, all the old fluency\u2019s disappeared. I don\u2019t write a single sentence without saying to myself, \u2018It\u2019s a lie!\u2019 So I know I was right. It\u2019s the best chance I\u2019ve ever had.',
